{
  "id": "e05",
  "rule": "media upload refusals before anything is stored: the create permission chain in WordPress's order (id, author, sticky, upload_files, the parent, the declared image type), the parent's type (an attachment; a revision has no post id in QuarkPress, D31), multipart bodies without a usable file part (another name, file[] and file[a], an empty file name), Content-MD5 forms, the raw body's header checks and file name, JSON bodies (url included, D39) and unreadable multipart bodies; the collection's Allow following the create check (r21); then uploads both sides store (req48 on): fields a failed preparation drops but the caption (r01), featured media after the row (r03, r04, S13), statuses (r16); how the create permission reads a refused upload's generate_sub_sizes in its image check (a TIFF no editor sizes, refused by its status: \"false\", \"0\", absent), a whole 201 (r26), the raw bodies the header table accepts (r06; an empty Content-Type line, the last Content-Disposition line, a name cut at its semicolon, a path dropped, a name taken twice), fields in the query string, the post fields of a multipart upload, a PDF, a video and a template; images without sizes (generate_sub_sizes=false), so a WordPress without an image editor compares",
